# Phase 18 NameServer configuration RPC slice — 2026-10-21T06:09:54Z

- Continued the pinned RocketMQ Java 5.5.1 audit at source commit
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`. Added Core mappings for
  `MQClientAPIImpl.updateNameServerConfig(Properties,List,long)`, request 318,
  and `getNameServerConfig(List,long)`, request 319.
- Updates serialize UTF-8 `key=value\n` properties, skip empty inputs, select
  explicit or configured NameServers, call every server in list order, and
  report the last non-success response. Reads query each server in order,
  parse Java Properties into an address-keyed map, preserve malformed property
  content as null map values, and stop at the first response error. No selected
  servers produce a no-op update or null read. Invoked Java fixtures and Rust
  differentials cover signatures, request envelopes, per-server body/results,
  list fallback, error ordering, malformed properties and missing bodies.
  Java throws `NullPointerException` for a successful read without a body;
  Rust returns structured `MalformedResponse`. Producer core fixture SHA-256:
  `4276123552ab57632da4a10177b1b529266707234e95785668cfcd12177e783c`.
